window.LEARN_CONTENT=window.LEARN_CONTENT||{};window.LEARN_CONTENT["a-fb711a5bf3ce0f35"]={"zh":"<p><a id=\"build-react-native-apps-with-expo\"></a></p> <h1 id=\"expo-react-native\">使用 Expo 构建 React Native 应用</h1> <p>使用专用插件，将移动应用想法转化为可运行的 Expo 应用。</p> <p>使用 Codex 和 Expo 插件搭建 React Native 应用，遵循 Expo Router 和 Expo 原生软件包惯例；先快速测试，仅当应用确实需要时，再使用开发客户端或 EAS 构建。</p> <p><a id=\"best-for\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_1\">适合哪些情况</h2> <ul> <li>希望先使用 Expo 对 React Native 应用进行原型设计或发布，再考虑原生 IDE 工作流的开发者。</li> <li>希望 Codex 遵循 Expo 路由、UI、软件包安装、构建和部署惯例的 Expo Router 项目。</li> <li>需要将 Web 应用迁移为移动应用的开发者。</li> </ul> <p><a id=\"skills-plugins\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_2\">技能与插件</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>技能或插件</th> <th>用途</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">expo（需联网）</a></td> <td>使用 Expo 编写的技能，了解 Expo Router UI、原生风格组件、数据获取、开发客户端、部署、升级、模块，以及 Codex Run 操作接入。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_3\">技术栈建议</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>需求</th> <th>建议选择</th> <th>原因</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>移动应用框架</td> <td><a href=\"https://expo.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo（需联网）</a> 和 <a href=\"https://reactnative.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">React Native（需联网）</a></td> <td>Expo 为 Codex 提供了由 Expo 管理的 React Native 开发路径，支持快速迭代、兼容的软件包和部署工具。</td> </tr> <tr> <td>路由</td> <td><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/router/introduction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo Router（需联网）</a></td> <td>Expo Router 通过文件组织路由，使导航清晰、可预测，帮助 Codex 添加页面和流程，而不必另造路由层。</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <p><a id=\"starter-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_4\">起步提示词</h2> <p>构建 Expo 应用</p> <p>建议推理级别：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">请使用 Expo 插件，根据以下想法构建 React Native 应用：\n\n[describe the app idea, target users, and the main workflow]（描述应用想法、目标用户和主要工作流程）\n\n要求：\n- 从 Expo Router 和 Expo 原生项目惯例开始。\n- 先尝试运行 `npx expo start` 并使用 Expo Go，再考虑自定义构建。\n- 添加 Expo 软件包时使用 `npx expo install`，以保持依赖兼容。\n- 导航、表单、列表、空状态和加载状态应采用符合原生应用习惯的 UI 模式。\n\n交付内容：\n- 可运行的应用功能切片\n- 运行命令\n- 使用的验证流程，包括 Expo Go、设备、模拟器、开发客户端或 EAS\n</code></pre> <p><a id=\"related-links\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_5\">关联文档</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo 插件（需联网）</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/eas/ai/mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo MCP 服务器设置（需联网）</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>完整文档索引请参阅 <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt（需联网）</a>。在文档页面 URL 末尾添加 <code>.md</code>，即可获取该页面的 Markdown 版本。</p> </blockquote> <p><a id=\"start-with-expo-go\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"expo-go\">从 Expo Go 开始</h2> <p>如果希望 Codex 将移动应用想法转化为经过测试的 React Native 应用，Expo 是很好的默认选择。推荐的流程是先运行 <code>expo start</code>，再在设备上使用 Expo Go；只有当应用需要自定义原生代码、应用商店分发，或 Expo Go 无法运行的能力时，才改用开发客户端或 EAS 构建。</p> <p>这样可以让 Codex 专注于应用工作流程，而不必在第一轮就花时间配置原生 IDE、模拟器、签名配置文件或构建参数。</p> <p><a id=\"use-the-expo-plugin\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"expo\">使用 Expo 插件</h2> <p>Expo 发布了一个 <a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo 插件（需联网）</a>，为 Codex 提供 Expo 原生开发指南，涵盖 Expo Router、原生 UI、表单、导航、动画、数据获取、NativeWind 设置、Expo 模块、开发客户端、部署、升级和 Codex Run 操作接入。</p> <p>在 Codex 构建新的 Expo 页面、添加软件包、连接 API、准备开发客户端，或为 TestFlight、App Store、Play Store 或 EAS Hosting 准备应用时，都可以使用它。</p> <p>如果任务需要查询最新 Expo 文档、安装兼容的软件包、运行 EAS 构建和工作流操作、采集截图、操作模拟器、使用 React Native DevTools 或查看 TestFlight 数据，也可以选择添加 <a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/eas/ai/mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo MCP Server（需联网）</a>。</p> <p><a id=\"iteration-process\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_6\">迭代流程</h2> <ol> <li>让 Codex 检查代码库，并确认这是一个新的 Expo 应用，还是已有的 Expo 项目。</li> <li>从 Expo Router 和 Expo Go 开始；添加 Expo 软件包时使用 <code>npx expo install</code>。</li> <li>让 Codex 构建一条完整的工作流程，其中应包括符合原生应用习惯的导航、加载状态、空状态和错误状态。</li> <li>通过最快的可用方式验证，例如在设备上的 Expo Go 或模拟器中验证；只有在需要时才改用开发客户端或 EAS。</li> </ol> <p><a id=\"suggested-follow-up-prompt\"></a></p> <h2 id=\"_7\">建议的后续提示词</h2> <p><strong>提示词：</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Expo plugin to add the following [feature/screen/flow] to this app:\n\n[describe one feature, screen or user flow]\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Keep Expo Router as the routing layer.\n- Use Expo-compatible package installs.\n- Test with Expo Go first.\n- Move to dev client or EAS only if this feature requires it.\n\nAfter implementing, tell me the exact run path you used and what you verified.\n</code></pre><div class=\"prompt-translation\"><div class=\"prompt-reference-heading\"><strong>提示词中文参考</strong><button class=\"copy-code copy-prompt-translation\" type=\"button\" aria-label=\"复制中文参考\">复制中文</button></div><div class=\"prompt-reference-text\">使用 Expo 插件，为这个应用添加以下 [feature/screen/flow]：\n\n[describe one feature, screen or user flow]\n\n约束：\n\n- 继续使用 Expo Router 作为路由层。\n- 使用与 Expo 兼容的软件包安装方式。\n- 先用 Expo Go 测试。\n- 只有这项功能确实需要时，才转用 dev client 或 EAS。\n\n实现后，告诉我你实际采用的运行路径，以及验证了什么。</div></div>","en":"<h1 id=\"build-react-native-apps-with-expo\">Build React Native apps with Expo</h1> <p>Go from a mobile-app idea to a working Expo app with the dedicated plugin.</p> <p>Use Codex with the Expo plugin to scaffold React Native apps, stay inside Expo Router and Expo-native package conventions, test quickly with Expo Go, and move to dev clients or EAS builds only when the app needs them.</p> <h2 id=\"best-for\">Best for</h2> <ul> <li>Developers who want to prototype or ship a React Native app with Expo before reaching for native IDE workflows.</li> <li>Expo Router projects where Codex should follow Expo conventions for routing, UI, package installs, builds, and deployment.</li> <li>Developers that need to migrate a web app to a mobile app.</li> </ul> <h2 id=\"skills-plugins\">Skills &amp; Plugins</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Skill or plugin</th> <th>Why use it</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">expo (online)</a></td> <td>Use Expo-authored skills for Expo Router UI, native-feeling components, data fetching, dev clients, deployment, upgrades, modules, and Codex Run action wiring.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"tech-stack-recommendations\">Tech stack recommendations</h2> <table> <thead> <tr> <th>Need</th> <th>Good default</th> <th>Why</th> </tr> </thead> <tbody> <tr> <td>Mobile framework</td> <td><a href=\"https://expo.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo (online)</a> and <a href=\"https://reactnative.dev/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">React Native (online)</a></td> <td>Expo gives Codex a managed React Native path with fast iteration, compatible packages, and deployment tooling.</td> </tr> <tr> <td>Routing</td> <td><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/router/introduction/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo Router (online)</a></td> <td>Expo Router keeps navigation file-based and predictable, which helps Codex add screens and flows without inventing a custom routing layer.</td> </tr> </tbody> </table> <h2 id=\"starter-prompt\">Starter prompt</h2> <p>Build the Expo App</p> <p>Suggested reasoning effort：<code>medium</code></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Expo plugin to build a React Native app with Expo for this idea:\n\n[describe the app idea, target users, and the main workflow]\n\nRequirements:\n- Start with Expo Router and Expo-native project conventions.\n- Try `npx expo start` and Expo Go first before creating a custom build.\n- Use `npx expo install` for Expo packages so dependencies stay compatible.\n- Use native-feeling UI patterns for navigation, forms, lists, empty states, and loading states.\n\nDeliver:\n- the working app slice\n- the run command\n- the verification path you used, including Expo Go, device, simulator, dev client, or EAS\n</code></pre> <h2 id=\"related-links\">Related links</h2> <ul> <li><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo plugin (online)</a></li> <li><a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/eas/ai/mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo MCP Server setup (online)</a></li> </ul> <blockquote> <p>For the complete documentation index, see <a href=\"https://learn.chatgpt.com/llms.txt\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">llms.txt (online)</a>. Markdown versions of documentation pages are available by appending <code>.md</code> to the page URL.</p> </blockquote> <h2 id=\"start-with-expo-go\">Start with Expo Go</h2> <p>Expo is a strong default when you want Codex to move from a mobile-app idea to a tested React Native app. The useful loop is <code>expo start</code> first, Expo Go on a device next, and then a dev client or EAS build only when the app needs custom native code, store distribution, or a capability that Expo Go can't run.</p> <p>That keeps Codex focused on the app workflow instead of spending the first pass on native IDE setup, simulator setup, provisioning, or build configuration.</p> <h2 id=\"use-the-expo-plugin\">Use the Expo plugin</h2> <p>Expo published an <a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/skills/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo plugin (online)</a> that gives Codex Expo-native guidance for Expo Router, native UI, forms, navigation, animations, data fetching, NativeWind setup, Expo modules, dev clients, deployment, upgrades, and Codex Run action wiring.</p> <p>Use it when Codex is building new Expo screens, adding packages, wiring API calls, preparing a dev client, or getting an app ready for TestFlight, App Store, Play Store, or EAS Hosting.</p> <p>Optionally, add the <a href=\"https://docs.expo.dev/eas/ai/mcp/\" target=\"_blank\" rel=\"noopener noreferrer\">Expo MCP Server (online)</a> when the task needs current Expo documentation lookup, compatible package installation, EAS build and workflow operations, screenshots, simulator interaction, React Native DevTools, or TestFlight data.</p> <h2 id=\"iteration-process\">Iteration process</h2> <ol> <li>Ask Codex to inspect the repo and confirm whether it is a new Expo app or an existing Expo project.</li> <li>Start with Expo Router and Expo Go, and use <code>npx expo install</code> when adding Expo packages.</li> <li>Ask Codex to build one complete workflow with native-feeling navigation, loading states, empty states, and error states.</li> <li>Verify on the fastest available path, such as Expo Go on a device or a simulator, then move to a dev client or EAS only when needed.</li> </ol> <h2 id=\"suggested-follow-up-prompt\">Suggested follow-up prompt</h2> <p><strong>Prompt:</strong></p> <pre><code class=\"language-text\">Use the Expo plugin to add the following [feature/screen/flow] to this app:\n\n[describe one feature, screen or user flow]\n\nConstraints:\n\n- Keep Expo Router as the routing layer.\n- Use Expo-compatible package installs.\n- Test with Expo Go first.\n- Move to dev client or EAS only if this feature requires it.\n\nAfter implementing, tell me the exact run path you used and what you verified.\n</code></pre>"};
